  "verdict": "NEGATIVE on net benefit: no override threshold yields meaningful net gain. The only positive net (+0.5 at margin 6.0) occurs where h_phi overrides 8.8 of ~415 states, i.e. has stopped acting. h_phi DID learn (contrastive 66% vs 21% random; harmful 13.8% vs 27% random; monotone with data), but discrimination is not sharp enough to act on. Structural cause: the harmful-exposure population (158) is 4x the rescue population (36), so precision dominates. Explicit rollout never faced this because policy improvement guaranteed it never harmed. NOT SATURATED: rescue ranking still climbing at the largest subset, so this is data- or capacity-limited rather than proof the value is unlearnable."
